/**
 * HOW TALL EACH CHARACTER IS DRAWN, in source pixels: the tallest frame it
 * has. The pack is not one resolution — the legacy sprites are 22 px people
 * and the new ones are rendered at ten times that — so the renderer cannot
 * have one scale. It asks for a HEIGHT ON SCREEN and divides by this.
 *
 * Per CHARACTER and not per frame, deliberately: a passing pose is taller
 * than a stride, and that difference IS the walk cycle. Scaling each frame to
 * the same height would iron it flat.
 */
